1
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,790
In the year 850, the Colossal Titan
reappeared and demolished another wall.

2
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:29,450
Once again, humanity allowed
the Titans to further their advance.

3
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:33,620
One after another,
soldiers fell to the Titans.

4
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:35,250
And then...

5
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:36,410
Eren!

6
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:37,870
Hurry!

7
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:48,080
Eren fell prey to a Titan too.

8
00:00:48,910 --> 00:00:51,450
Man, Mikasa's incredible...

9
00:00:51,450 --> 00:00:53,700
How can she move so fast?!

10
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:56,790
No! She's not her usual,
composed self at all!

11
00:00:56,790 --> 00:00:58,870
I'll do whatever it takes to win!

12
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:01,120
Whatever it takes to live!

13
00:01:01,910 --> 00:01:05,000
Mikasa found herself in
dire straits as well

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,700
when a mysterious Titan
appeared and attacked another Titan.

15
00:01:31,790 --> 00:01:36,830
<i>Unknown are the names</i>
<i>of the flowers that have been trampled</i>

16
00:01:36,830 --> 00:01:42,290
<i>Birds have fallen to the earth</i>
<i>and long for the wind</i>

17
00:01:42,290 --> 00:01:47,370
<i>Prayers won't solve anything</i>

18
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:52,700
<i>Only the will to fight</i>
<i>can change the here and now!</i>

19
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:58,000
<i>O pigs who laugh at the resolve</i>
<i>to walk over corpses to move forward</i>

20
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,540
<i>Livestock complacency? False prosperity?</i>

21
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:03,450
<i>Give us the freedom of dying,</i>
<i>starving wolves!</i>

22
00:02:03,450 --> 00:02:08,830
<i>The humiliation of being caged</i>
<i>is what triggers us to fight back</i>

23
00:02:08,830 --> 00:02:14,120
<i>We hunters slaughter prey</i>
<i>beyond the castle walls,</i>

24
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:19,330
<i>consumed with surging bloodlust,</i>

25
00:02:19,330 --> 00:02:26,250
<i>as our crimson bows and arrows</i>
<i>pierce scarlet holes into the twilight</i>

26
00:02:48,450 --> 00:02:53,330
"I Can Hear His Heartbeat"
"The Struggle for Trost, Part 4"

27
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:55,250
There!

28
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:58,910
Your mobility gear still works,
and I've given you all my blades.

29
00:02:58,910 --> 00:03:02,500
All I ask is that you
leave me with this one...

30
00:03:03,370 --> 00:03:07,660
I'd rather not get
eaten alive, if I can help it.

31
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:15,660
N-No way...

32
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:18,120
Armin.

33
00:03:20,330 --> 00:03:22,910
I'm not leaving you here.

34
00:03:26,290 --> 00:03:29,660
B-But the place is swarming with Titans;

35
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:31,870
you can't possibly
carry someone while jumping--

36
00:03:31,870 --> 00:03:33,290
Let's go!

37
00:03:34,950 --> 00:03:36,750
No...

38
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:38,370
Please don't...

39
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:40,830
I'll only...

40
00:03:40,830 --> 00:03:44,040
I'll only get more of my friends killed!

41
00:03:55,290 --> 00:03:56,500
Wait!

42
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:59,000
Listen! I have a suggestion!

43
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,620
A suggestion?

44
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:07,160
Only you two can do it,
so I leave the choice to you...

45
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:09,500
I know it sounds crazy,

46
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:11,620
but could we use
that Titan to our advantage?

47
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:13,120
That Titan?!

48
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:17,250
It attacks other Titans and
doesn't show any interest in us.

49
00:04:17,250 --> 00:04:22,120
So I'm wondering if we
could lead it to the supply building...

50
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:27,250
If it takes out the other Titans
for us, we just might all survive!

51
00:04:27,250 --> 00:04:31,250
<i>Lead </i>it?! How do you
hope to lead that thing?!

52
00:04:31,250 --> 00:04:34,250
My guess is it's fighting on instinct.

53
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:38,290
If you two take out the Titans around it,

54
00:04:38,290 --> 00:04:42,120
it'll go and look for other Titans.

55
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:44,410
That'll naturally lead
it toward Headquarters.

56
00:04:44,410 --> 00:04:48,040
W-We can't risk our
necks for some hopeful guess!

57
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:51,080
But if it works, we could eliminate
all the Titans attacking HQ

58
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:53,040
in one fell swoop!

59
00:04:54,790 --> 00:04:57,040
--It seems worth trying.
--Huh?!

60
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:58,620
Are you serious?!

61
00:04:58,620 --> 00:05:03,040
It's better to take a gamble than
wait for our inevitable deaths.

62
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:05,620
Let's go with Armin's suggestion.

63
00:05:05,620 --> 00:05:08,620
You want us to
fight Titans <i>with </i>a Titan?!

64
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:10,620
Yes. I do.

65
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:16,250
If we fail, we'll be laughingstocks.

66
00:05:17,370 --> 00:05:20,750
But if we succeed, everyone survives.

67
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:22,750
It all comes down to resolve.

68
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:26,660
All right! Fine!

69
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:35,080
Am I really cut out for this?

70
00:05:36,330 --> 00:05:41,000
Am I really fit to have
a position of responsibility?

71
00:05:45,790 --> 00:05:47,500
No!

72
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:51,120
No... <i>now </i>is the time.

73
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:55,540
Now is our chance, while the
Titans are preoccupied over there!

74
00:05:57,830 --> 00:05:59,250
Now!

75
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:02,750
Make for HQ while we have the chance!

76
00:06:13,450 --> 00:06:14,950
Now is our only chance!

77
00:06:14,950 --> 00:06:18,290
If we run out of gas,
it's all over anyway!

78
00:06:18,290 --> 00:06:20,120
Everyone, charge!

79
00:07:07,250 --> 00:07:08,870
--Jean!
--Huh?

80
00:07:08,870 --> 00:07:11,870
Thanks! You helped us get away!

81
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:13,080
Huh?!

82
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,330
It's all thanks to you!

83
00:07:14,330 --> 00:07:19,000
It's like I said before!
You make a good leader!

84
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,700
I'm not so sure about that!

85
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,120
Damn!

86
00:07:50,330 --> 00:07:52,620
How many made it?

87
00:07:55,330 --> 00:07:57,580
How many comrades' deaths did I use?!

88
00:07:57,580 --> 00:08:01,790
How many people
died because of my orders?

89
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:15,080
You're with the
supply team, aren't you?

90
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:16,540
Yeah...

91
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:20,950
Stop, Jean!

92
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:24,080
<i>These </i>are the ones who abandoned us!

93
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:27,000
People are dead because of you guys!

94
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,830
The Titans overran the supply room!

95
00:08:29,830 --> 00:08:31,410
There was nothing we could do!

96
00:08:31,410 --> 00:08:34,750
It's <i>your </i>job to deal with it anyway!

97
00:08:37,750 --> 00:08:39,370
Hit the deck!

98
00:08:44,910 --> 00:08:46,120
Crap...!

99
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:49,750
There are too many people!

100
00:08:49,750 --> 00:08:51,120
--Hurry!
--Get further inside!

101
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,000
Stop! We can't <i>all </i>go at once!

102
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,580
Where'd Mikasa go?!

103
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:58,080
She ran out of gas!
She's long gone by now!

104
00:08:58,410 --> 00:09:00,250
<i>This </i>is normal...

105
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:03,580
<i>This </i>must be what the real world is like...

106
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:08,290
Was I trying to
delude myself up until now?

107
00:09:08,290 --> 00:09:13,410
Surely I knew what
the real world was like...

108
00:09:13,410 --> 00:09:17,250
It's so obvious when you think about it...

109
00:09:17,910 --> 00:09:22,830
There's no way we stand a
chance against these monstrosities...

110
00:09:31,660 --> 00:09:33,080
What?!

111
00:09:43,870 --> 00:09:45,410
Huh?

112
00:09:45,410 --> 00:09:47,330
What the hell...?

113
00:09:51,450 --> 00:09:52,540
Mikasa!

114
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:55,790
Man, that was close.
It's completely empty.

115
00:09:55,790 --> 00:09:59,200
We did it! We managed to make it!

116
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:02,450
Wh-Whoa, you're alive!

117
00:10:02,450 --> 00:10:04,000
--We did it, Armin!
--O-Ouch!

118
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,830
Your plan worked!

119
00:10:06,830 --> 00:10:07,830
Guys!

120
00:10:07,830 --> 00:10:11,000
That Titan's an Abnormal!
It's killin' all the other Titans!

121
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,330
<i>And </i>it has no interest in us!

122
00:10:14,330 --> 00:10:18,160
We can use it to our
advantage to escape from here!

123
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:21,500
Use a Titan?!

124
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:24,080
A Titan, helping us?!

125
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:27,750
--What kind of nonsensical dream--
--It's no dream.

126
00:10:27,750 --> 00:10:30,290
Whether it's an Abnormal
or not, I don't care.

127
00:10:30,290 --> 00:10:34,580
We're going to let it rampage
here for as long as possible.

128
00:10:38,620 --> 00:10:45,330
Because, realistically, that's our
best strategy for survival now.

129
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:08,410
It's okay.

130
00:11:08,410 --> 00:11:11,700
That Titan's tougher than ordinary ones.

131
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:18,120
I doubt they'll take down this building

132
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:22,410
while that one's rampaging like crazy.

133
00:11:22,410 --> 00:11:26,620
How much do you know about that Titan?

134
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:30,910
We can worry about that <i>after </i>we're safe.

135
00:11:30,910 --> 00:11:34,290
Yeah. Let's survive first.

136
00:11:34,290 --> 00:11:36,040
We found some!

137
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:38,660
They belong to the Military Police!

138
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:41,450
Damn things are all covered in dust...

139
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:46,040
Are you sure buckshot
is what we want to use?!

140
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:48,750
I mean, seriously...

141
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:52,830
Will guns even work against Titans?

142
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:57,410
They're far better than nothing, I feel.

143
00:11:57,410 --> 00:12:01,540
If there are still seven Titans in the supply
room that are three or four meters tall,

144
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:06,790
this much firepower should be capable
of blinding them all simultaneously.

145
00:12:06,790 --> 00:12:11,410
First, we'll use the lift to lower a
group of people from the center ceiling.

146
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:15,950
They'll then simultaneously fire
at the faces of each of the seven Titans,

147
00:12:15,950 --> 00:12:17,750
thereby blinding them.

148
00:12:17,750 --> 00:12:22,750
Then comes the moment of truth...

149
00:12:22,750 --> 00:12:24,700
Seven people hiding up top

150
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:29,040
will strike the Titans'
vitals just after the guns fire.

151
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:34,120
In other words, this plan
will put everything on the line--

152
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:36,250
everyone's lives on the line--

153
00:12:36,250 --> 00:12:37,870
for a single attack.

154
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:44,330
Seven people will have to slay seven
Titans at the same time in a single blow.

155
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:51,040
It'll be up to the seven most physically
fit and adept soldiers we have here.

156
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:56,830
So, umm, I'm sorry for placing
everyone's lives on your shoulders...

157
00:12:56,830 --> 00:12:58,290
It's no problem.

158
00:12:58,290 --> 00:13:02,620
If we fail, we die. The risk's
the same regardless of who goes.

159
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:09,540
Still, is this shabby idea of
mine really our best strategy?

160
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:15,290
We got no other choice.
We're out of time and options.

161
00:13:15,290 --> 00:13:17,450
All we can do now is give it our all!

162
00:13:17,450 --> 00:13:21,200
It'll be fine. Be confident.

163
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:23,750
You have a knack for
figuring out correct solutions.

164
00:13:23,750 --> 00:13:24,790
Huh?

165
00:13:24,790 --> 00:13:28,790
You even used it to save
my life and Eren's life before.

166
00:13:28,790 --> 00:13:32,410
It did...? When?

167
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:35,540
The lift's ready!

168
00:13:35,540 --> 00:13:38,370
The guns too! They're all loaded!

169
00:13:38,370 --> 00:13:40,290
You just don't realize it.

170
00:13:40,290 --> 00:13:42,450
--We can talk about it later.
--Yeah.

171
00:13:44,870 --> 00:13:50,330
Still, can we really take out all
the Titans without our ODM gear?

172
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:51,660
Of course we can!

173
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,910
These Titans are only three or four meters tall.

174
00:13:53,910 --> 00:13:56,160
Targeting their vitals will be a cinch.

175
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:57,250
Yeah.

176
00:13:57,250 --> 00:14:01,290
Regardless of size, their vitals go
from the head to the nape of the neck...

177
00:14:01,290 --> 00:14:04,290
...one meter high and ten centimeters across!

178
00:14:04,290 --> 00:14:07,410
You can also shove
one of these up their asses!

179
00:14:07,410 --> 00:14:09,500
Those are their only two weak spots!

180
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:12,290
I never knew about that one!

181
00:14:12,290 --> 00:14:15,080
This is the first I've heard of it, too.

182
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:16,580
Reiner.

183
00:14:16,580 --> 00:14:20,290
Those <i>could </i>end up
being your last words, you know.

184
00:14:33,580 --> 00:14:36,500
Good. Their numbers haven't increased.

185
00:14:41,950 --> 00:14:44,500
Proceeding with operation!

186
00:14:53,580 --> 00:14:57,040
Stay clam! We need
to lure them all the way in!

187
00:15:01,370 --> 00:15:02,790
Steady...

188
00:15:05,290 --> 00:15:08,120
Avoid a disadvantageous fight...

189
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:10,830
If you don't want <i>anyone </i>to die...

190
00:15:10,830 --> 00:15:13,750
...then make this attack count!

191
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:16,500
Steady...

192
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:25,450
Ready...

193
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,620
Fire!

194
00:15:41,790 --> 00:15:42,790
I got mine!

195
00:15:42,790 --> 00:15:44,910
How about you guys?!

196
00:15:53,370 --> 00:15:55,200
U-Umm...

197
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:58,250
--I'm sorry for suddenly sneaking up and...
--C-Crap...

198
00:15:58,250 --> 00:16:00,950
I'm very sorry...!

199
00:16:00,950 --> 00:16:02,330
Sasha and Conny!

200
00:16:02,330 --> 00:16:04,450
Hurry! Lend them backup!

201
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:10,080
I'm... umm...

202
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:12,080
I'm very sorry!

203
00:16:23,830 --> 00:16:26,200
Mikasa!

204
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:28,540
You saved me!

205
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:29,660
Are you all right?

206
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:30,790
Thanks to you!

207
00:16:30,790 --> 00:16:32,370
Then get up.

208
00:16:32,370 --> 00:16:33,950
I owe you one...

209
00:16:33,950 --> 00:16:35,000
No problem.

210
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
Oh, man.

211
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,120
That was a close call, Annie.

212
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:41,870
I'm really glad you didn't end up hurt.

213
00:16:41,870 --> 00:16:44,000
They've all been slain!

214
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,580
Switch to resupply work!

215
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:47,410
We did it!

216
00:16:52,790 --> 00:16:56,580
--All right! We're gonna survive!
--And no more Titans are coming inside!

217
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:59,700
All thanks to that
berserk Titan out there!

218
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:04,000
I caved in to that Titan...

219
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,120
I'm too ashamed to face the others...!

220
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:08,120
There'll be plenty of
time to sneer at you later!

221
00:17:08,120 --> 00:17:09,700
For now, we gotta escape!

222
00:17:10,750 --> 00:17:14,330
I can't see myself as much of a leader.

223
00:17:14,330 --> 00:17:16,620
Don't talk like that anymore.

224
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:23,580
I don't mean any offense by this,

225
00:17:23,580 --> 00:17:26,580
but I think the fact you <i>aren't </i>strong

226
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:29,410
really lets you understand
how the weak feel.

227
00:17:29,410 --> 00:17:33,910
And your skill at recognizing
a situation as it unfolds

228
00:17:33,910 --> 00:17:37,870
gives you a clear grasp of what
needs to be done <i>now</i>, you know?

229
00:17:38,910 --> 00:17:41,370
You made the right call.

230
00:17:41,370 --> 00:17:45,200
It's what got me moving.
It's why I'm alive now.

231
00:17:50,950 --> 00:17:53,580
Everyone ready?! It's time to scram!

232
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:56,620
--Let's move!
--Scale the wall!

233
00:17:56,620 --> 00:17:58,620
Rendezvous with the main forces!

234
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:01,950
Mikasa?!

235
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:07,370
Mikasa!

236
00:18:07,370 --> 00:18:09,330
We have to get out of here!

237
00:18:09,330 --> 00:18:11,040
That Titan...

238
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:16,870
They're cannibalizing it?!

239
00:18:19,330 --> 00:18:22,080
I guess it can't regenerate its body?

240
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:27,000
I thought that if we could somehow
figure out what's up with that Titan,

241
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:32,410
it could've helped us break
free from this hopeless situation...

242
00:18:32,410 --> 00:18:34,330
I agree.

243
00:18:34,330 --> 00:18:38,200
We'll learn nothing at all
if it ends up getting eaten!

244
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:42,370
For now, we have to get
rid of the ones clinging to it

245
00:18:42,370 --> 00:18:43,950
and help keep it alive!

246
00:18:43,950 --> 00:18:45,370
Are you insane, Reiner?!

247
00:18:45,370 --> 00:18:48,200
We can finally get our asses out of here!

248
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:53,540
And what if there's a chance
that Titan could become our ally?

249
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:56,410
It'd be a more powerful weapon
than any cannon, wouldn't you agree?

250
00:18:57,540 --> 00:18:59,200
Ally...?

251
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:01,040
Are you actually serious?!

252
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:03,950
That one...!

253
00:19:04,620 --> 00:19:08,040
That's the Abnormal that ate Thomas!

254
00:19:41,620 --> 00:19:43,040
Oh, man...

255
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:50,870
What was it you wanted to save again?

256
00:19:57,580 --> 00:20:01,540
Looks like it's finished for good.

257
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:04,080
All right, that's enough! Let's get going!

258
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:06,950
As if that monster would ever be our ally...

259
00:20:06,950 --> 00:20:09,000
A Titan's a Titan.

260
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:15,580
What's with you guys?

261
00:20:39,450 --> 00:20:40,870
Mikasa!

262
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:52,040
It's Eren...

263
00:21:53,290 --> 00:21:59,200
His severed arm and leg are back...

264
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:04,410
He'd been swallowed by a Titan back then...

265
00:22:04,410 --> 00:22:05,830
Back then...

266
00:22:14,910 --> 00:22:18,450
How is this possible?

267
00:22:26,120 --> 00:22:33,250
Does this mean <i>Eren </i>did all this...?

268
00:22:52,910 --> 00:22:58,040
<i>Your dreams are where your heart is</i>

269
00:22:58,040 --> 00:23:04,290
<i>They're more fragile than life itself</i>

270
00:23:04,290 --> 00:23:08,950
<i>Over and over you cast them aside,</i>
<i>only to find more</i>

271
00:23:08,950 --> 00:23:15,620
<i>Now, rest in peace</i>

272
00:23:15,620 --> 00:23:26,950
<i>Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for</i>

273
00:23:26,950 --> 00:23:37,250
<i>and the more we forget</i>
<i>the more we remember again</i>

274
00:23:37,250 --> 00:23:43,200
<i>In this beautiful, cruel world</i>

275
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:48,370
<i>all I can do is ask why we're still alive</i>

276
00:23:48,370 --> 00:23:54,080
<i>Oh, with our strength--and our weakness--</i>

277
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:59,750
<i>what are we going to protect if there's no sense</i>

278
00:23:59,750 --> 00:24:03,160
<i>to anything anymore?</i>

279
00:24:09,500 --> 00:24:11,910
"I'm going to drive out the Titans."

280
00:24:11,910 --> 00:24:16,540
That strong emotion
transformed Eren into a Titan.

281
00:24:16,540 --> 00:24:19,500
However, the Garrison Regiment
deems him a threat to humanity

282
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:21,410
and turns its swords at him.

283
00:24:21,410 --> 00:24:23,370
"Whereabouts of His Left Arm"
"The Struggle for Trost, Part 5"
